cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this instrument, cite the version you ran; the research claim is registered in docs/2026-11-20-PREREG.md and is NOT yet supported by GPU-phase evidence."
title: "Psychopomp: identity-free possible-world filtering under occlusion"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic two-dimensional occluder simulator with an observable/oracle
  event split, a typed append-only event log, an EPEC-inspired possible-world
  filter over identity-free observations, a structure-preserving shuffled
  control, and pre-GPU CPU baselines. Publication is not a reuse grant: no
  license file is present, by operator decision.
authors:
